# "During your turn, this creature has first strike" (CR 613.1f, 702.7): the Spire has it only while it is Bot1's turn. Bot1 plays the Spire on turn 1 and on turn 4, Bot2's
# turn, pays {U}{R} and animates it (instant speed, CR 602.5d): it has no first strike now. Bot2 attacks with Llanowar Elves and Bot1 blocks with the Spire: both deal damage
# at the same time, so the 2/1 Spire dies to the Elves' 1 damage and kills them too.

[Bot1 Deck]
Restless Spire
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Llanowar Elves
Forest x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Restless Spire.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Restless Spire.Activate(Ability: Until end of turn)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Restless Spire.Types = Land; Creature
? Bot1.Battlefield.Restless Spire.Keywords = (absent)
Bot2.Attack(Llanowar Elves > Bot1)
Bot1.Block(Restless Spire > Llanowar Elves)
[T4 Bot2.Main2]
? Bot1.Graveyard = Restless Spire
? Bot2.Graveyard = Llanowar Elves
? Bot1.Life = 20

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Restless Spire
Bot2.Graveyard = Llanowar Elves
